{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And let not Elohim speak with us</b>. The Rav in the Guide for the Perplexed (3:33) took note of Onkelos (Onkelos on Exodus 20:16), who translated <b>וְאַל יְדַבֵּר עִמָּנוּ אֱלֹהִים</b> as “וְאַל יִתְמַלַּל עִמַּנָא מִן קֳדָם ה׳” (“And let Him not speak with us from before YHWH”), yet did not do so in other places, for he translated “וַיְדַבֵּר אֱלֹהִים אֵת כָּל הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה” (Exodus 20:1) as “וּמַלֵּל ה׳”, and likewise in every place, “וַיְדַבֵּר ה׳ אֶל מֹשֶׁה” — “וּמַלֵּל ה׳”. And the reason according to him is that the first utterance, even though all Israel heard it, their rank in it is not like the rank of Moses our teacher. If so, according to his own opinion, why did he translate “כִּי מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם דִּבַּרְתִּי עִמָּכֶם” (Exodus 20:22) as “מַלֵּלִית עִמְּכוֹן”, when he should have said “אִתְמַלַּל מִן קֳדָמַי עִמְּכוֹן”? And likewise in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 5:19), “אֶת הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה דִּבֶּר ה׳ אֶל כָּל קְהַלְכֶם” — he translated it “מַלֵּל ה׳”, and they themselves said “וְאֶת קוֹלוֹ שָׁמַעְנוּ” (Deuteronomy 5:21), and he translated “יָת קָל מֵימְרֵהּ שְׁמַעְנָא יוֹמָא דֵּין חֲזֵינָא אֲרֵי יְמַלֵּל ה׳ עִם אִינָשָׁא”, and likewise “פָּנִים בְּפָנִים דִּבֶּר ה׳ עִמָּכֶם” (Deuteronomy 5:4) — “מַלֵּל ה׳”. And furthermore, he translated “וְהָאֱלֹהִים יַעֲנֶנּוּ בְּקוֹל” (above, Exodus 19:19) as “וּמִן קֳדָם ה׳ מִתְעַנֵּי לֵיהּ בְּקָל”, and it has already come in the language of the Torah thus concerning Moses himself: “וַיִּשְׁמַע אֶת הַקּוֹל מִדַּבֵּר אֵלָיו” (Numbers 7:89), and its translation is “מִתְמַלַּל”, and likewise “יֵרֵד עַמּוּד הֶעָנָן וְעָמַד פֶּתַח הָאֹהֶל וְדִבֶּר עִם מֹשֶׁה” (Exodus 33:9) — “וּמִתְמַלַּל”.<br>But the reason for Onkelos is clarified: in all of the giving of the Torah, the speech of the Name to Israel is said to have come only from within the fire (Deuteronomy 5:21), and from the fire they heard, and that is what they perceived. And likewise “כִּי מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם” (Exodus 20:19), by way of truth, means from within the heavens, and that is the same as from within the fire — and its matter has already been explained (Ramban on Exodus 19:20). Now when Onkelos saw here <b>וְאַל יְדַבֵּר עִמָּנוּ אֱלֹהִים</b>, in which no medium is mentioned, he did not see fit to translate it as “וְלָא יְמַלֵּל עִמַּנָא ה׳”, for there is in his language no designation for the word “אֱלֹהִים”, and therefore he stripped from it the direct speech entirely.<br>And among the wonders of Onkelos’s wisdom is that at the standing at Mount Sinai he did not mention “יְקָרָא דַּה׳” (“the glory of YHWH”) or “מֵימְרָא דַּה׳” (“the Memra of YHWH”), but translated “הָא אֲנָא מִתְגְּלֵי לָךְ” (Exodus 19:9), “יִתְגְּלֵי ה׳ לְעֵינֵי כָל עַמָּא עַל טוּרָא דְּסִינָי” (Exodus 19:11), “דְּאִתְגְּלִי עֲלוֹהִי” (Exodus 19:18), “וְאִתְגְּלִי ה׳ עַל טוּרָא דְּסִינַי” (Exodus 19:20) — and did not translate “וְאִתְגְּלִי יְקָרָא דַּה׳” as he translates at the beginning, “הַר הָאֱלֹהִים” (Exodus 3:1) — “טוּרָא דְּאִיתְגְּלִי עֲלוֹהִי יְקָרָא דַּה׳”. So he did in every place where the unique Name is mentioned in connection with this descent. But when Scripture mentions “אֱלֹהִים”, he translated “לִקְרַאת הָאֱלֹהִים” (Onkelos on Exodus 19:17) — “לְקַדָּמוּת מֵימְרָא דַּה׳”, and translated “בָּא הָאֱלֹהִים” (Exodus 20:17) — “יִתְגְּלֵי לְכוֹן יְקָרָא דַּה׳”, and did not say “יִתְגְּלֵי לְכוֹן ה׳”, “דְּתַמָּן יְקָרָא דַּה׳” (Exodus 19:18), and likewise he said “וּמִן קֳדָם ה׳ מִתְעֲנֵי לֵיהּ בְּקָל” (above, Exodus 19:19). All this is clarified and spelled out for one who will understand our explicit words above (Exodus 19:20). And so I have seen in precise manuscripts: “וַיַּעַל מֹשֶׁה אֶל הַר הָאֱלֹהִים” (Exodus 24:13) — “וּסְלֵק מֹשֶׁה לְטוּרָא דַּה׳”, for after the giving of the Torah he says thus, as it is written “וַיִּסְעוּ מֵהַר ה׳” (Numbers 10:33)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The citation of the Guide for the Perplexed as (ב לג) appears to refer to part (or chapter) 33; the standard numbering of the relevant discussion is Guide 3:33 or the corresponding chapter in other divisions."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:13:01.798720437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}